<header class="docs-header">
  <p class="docs-eyebrow">Calico Melton</p>
  <h1>Design system</h1>
  <p class="docs-lede">The parts this shop is built from. Every page uses these and nothing else, so new pages need no new CSS.</p>
</header>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="layers">
  <h2 id="layers">How it fits together</h2>
  <ol class="docs-steps">
    <li><strong>Tokens</strong>: named values for colour, type, space and motion, written as DTCG JSON in <code>/tokens</code> and compiled to <code>--ds-*</code> custom properties. <a href="/design-system/tokens/">See the tokens</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Components</strong>: buttons, prices, the cart drawer and so on, each in <code>src/components/&lt;name&gt;/</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Patterns</strong>: components arranged into sections, like the collection grid or the Studio Letter band, each in <code>src/patterns/&lt;name&gt;/</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Pages</strong>: assembled from patterns.</li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="cascade">
  <h2 id="cascade">Cascade layers</h2>
  <p>All CSS ships in one file, in this order. A later layer always wins over an earlier one, whatever the selector.</p>
  <pre class="docs-code" tabindex="0"><code>@layer reset, tokens, base, components, patterns, utilities;</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="docs-section" aria-labelledby="components">
